Subject: [PATCH 112/274] TileLang V4.1 WO: WO-A on BF16 activations, as
 DeepSeek's reference

The reference dequantizes wo_a to BF16 (convert.py) and projects the BF16
attention output with an einsum; the TileLang WO quantized it to MXFP8 first.
A grouped W8A16 GEMM (fp8w_bf16_gemm) expands each FP8 weight tile exactly to
BF16 and accumulates in FP32, one launch for every group; row tiles of 16-128
share one K loop, so a row's bits do not depend on its batch. WO-B keeps the
reference's MXFP8 activations.

(cherry picked from commit 78edfe9e0f1736341a402ff1227a04cb00d8120c)

